{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused","id":1386870,"title":"Five Elemental Dragons: REALLY frustrated and confused?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T19:23:51-07:00","id":1386870,"title":"Five Elemental Dragons: REALLY frustrated and confused?","content":"I just read Technocracy Reloaded and I\u2019m really confused. Are the Five Elemental Dragons a good thing (because they show how different the Asian Technocracy is from its Western counterpart) or a bad thing (because they\u2019re stereotypes of Asians)?<br /> <br /> I might use them in a Mage game someday and the only East Asian guy in our group is Filipino and he was born in the US and doesn\u2019t really know or care either way and I just want it to be authentic. Please help if you have any advice. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:25:38-07:00","id":1386873,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know Taiping is the name of a 19th century Christian rebellion, but I figured it must mean SOMETHING else in Chinese too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:32:34-07:00","id":1386875,"title":"","content":"Nvm. I overreacted. They don\u2019t wanna eliminate the Dragons, just change their names to something less stereotypical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:57:13-07:00","id":1386882,"title":"","content":"I'm Filipino and have not had any problems with the Metal Dragons or most any mage group. Hope your game goes well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:21:16-07:00","id":1386889,"title":"","content":"Thank you \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:38:04-07:00","id":1386948,"title":"","content":"It's a quite contentious point.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Five Metal Dragons is what the *Shen* of the Middle Kingdom call the Technocracy. The Five Elemental Dragons are a sub conspiracy within the Five Metal Dragons. Technocracy Reloaded was basically giving the option for you to ignore the weird sub conspiracy bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:46:30-07:00","id":1386996,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26024_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26024\" data-vbnamecard=\"26024\">Distant Choir</a> Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. That clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:49:28-07:00","id":1387000,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26024_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26024\" data-vbnamecard=\"26024\">Distant Choir</a> did the Five Metal Dragons start in Asia independently of the Western Technocracy, or did they start when the Europeans penetrated into Asia in the 16th century?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:02:25-07:00","id":1387016,"title":"","content":"There is a thing in World of Darkness: Blood &amp; Silk (the Dark Ages book that looked at East Asia and the Shen around that time) about the Ministry of Works, a part of the Chinese imperial bureaucracy that was in charge of the Awakened. Basically, any Awakened that formally submitted to/registered with the Ministry and acknowledged the authority of the Emperor would find their magic to be consensual and work perfectly fine in China. The ultimate arbitrators of said Ministry are what we now know as the Wu Lung. (I can't recall when the Ministry's authority was officially broken; I know they were defunct by the time the Qing dynasty collapsed at the start of the 20th century, and I want to say that they were broken during or before the Opium Wars a century earlier, but I don't have the book handy and can't remember exactly.)<br /> <br /> My own head canon is that the Ministry had five branches - ie, five dragons that correspond to the five elements and directions - but around the 19th century, they split between the traditionalists who became the Wu Lung and those who decided to play a long game and adapt the Technocracy's methods and tools for its own and eventually perfect them so as to eventually reassert China's rightful place as the center of the world. These five elemental dragon groups still exist as regional sub-conspiracies within the Chinese Technocracy, but I do not use the names or group concepts presented in Dragons of the East, as some of them are non-sensical and in at least one case, a little offensive. I also have the Technocracy in Japan, South Korea, and other East Asian nations be unrelated to the former Ministry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:18:14-07:00","id":1387038,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of the Ministry of Works and I\u2019ve always been a big fan of the Wu Lung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:49:42-07:00","id":1387050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused#post1386870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read Technocracy Reloaded and I\u2019m really confused. Are the Five Elemental Dragons a good thing (because they show how different the Asian Technocracy is from its Western counterpart) or a bad thing (because they\u2019re stereotypes of Asians)?<br /> <br /> I might use them in a Mage game someday and the only East Asian guy in our group is Filipino and he was born in the US and doesn\u2019t really know or care either way and I just want it to be authentic. Please help if you have any advice. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> To both.<br /> <br /> The Five Metal Dragons is a terrible result of the Orientalist goofiness that was the Year of the Dragon where Asia was inserted like the Kingdom of Pandaria expansion to World of Warcraft. On the other hand, it did make the Technocracy less a bunch of white Europeans conquering the world [which isn't necessarily a bad thing if you ran the Traditions as partially resistance to colonialism].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:39:06-07:00","id":1387064,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> thank you. I think I\u2019m gonna leave the basic structure of the Five Dragons intact, except I\u2019m not going to make them a secret conspiracy against the rest of the Technocracy and I\u2019m gonna use the new names they suggest in Technocracy Reloaded.<br /> <br /> I feel better now. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T16:01:17-07:00","id":1388782,"title":"","content":"My thoughts about the Five Elemental Dragons<br /> <br /> The Five Elemental Dragons originally had the names given in Dragons of the East and were five independent groups of Asian willworkers who primarily encouraged the growth of science and reasons, as opposed to more mystically-oriented groups like the Akashayana and the Wu Lung. Three of them (the Zi Guang, the Miao Guan and the Taiping Tianguo) began in China, the other two (the Zaibatsu and the Saensaeng) began in Japan. <br /> <br /> When the Five Metal Dragons (the Conventions of the Order of Reason) came to Asia with the Europeans in the 1500s, these five groups felt like they needed to band together to resist European encroachment. In 1603 under the protection of the newly-formed Tokugawa Shogunate, they met in the city of Edo (now Tokyo) and became the Five Elemental Dragons. At that point they agreed to a relationship of equals with the Order of Reason and adopted the Dragon names given in Technocracy Reloaded. <br /> <br /> This relationship has been on again off again for the past four hundred and seventeen years, but at the moment the Dragons are pretty much in sync with the Western Technocracy. Not because they\u2019re forced to follow the party line, but because they see the Union as the best hope to bring peace and prosperity to the various peoples of east and Southeast Asia.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I don\u2019t know what any of the original names mean (except Zaibatsu, which means a large corporation). What do you guys think? I\u2019m definitely open to suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T16:26:15-07:00","id":1388787,"title":"","content":"You don't want to know my theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T17:13:20-07:00","id":1388793,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I wouldn\u2019t mind \ud83d\ude0a. It\u2019s okay if it\u2019s totally different from mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T17:43:02-07:00","id":1388799,"title":"","content":"Zaibatsu was a term for industrial/business conglomerates during Japan's imperial period (1868 - 1947) and were almost all forcefully dissolved or broken up by the Allied Occupation Forces after WW2. Modern Japanese business tends to involve Keiretsu, which are somewhat similar but are, in economic terms, horizontally integrated (meaning they tend to be a single group that controls most of the production of a single type of product - think how Disney controls such a huge chunk of the entertainment industry, or the way the Kraft Heinz Company controls a huge swath of the finished processed food market) rather than using the vertical integration (a single group that controls every single step of their product, such as the way Standard Oil owned it's entire process, from drilling to refining to transport to direct sales to customers). <br /> The name can make a certain amount of sense as a name the Japanese members of the Syndicate - or rather the Invisible Exchequer - used to refer to themselves after the Meiji Restoration, but after WW2, it'd be archaic, and any time before the 1870s would be anachronistic. <br /> <br /> As for Saensaeng, &quot;sean&quot;, depending on which characters are used, apparently either means &quot;tea plantation&quot; or &quot;to defer&quot; in Japanese. &quot;Saeng&quot; is apparently a Korean word that can mean student or to survive. However, there is a Korean term, Sangsaeng, that roughly means &quot;mutually life-giving&quot;. Its apparently frequently used by South Korean politicians to mean &quot;win-win&quot;, as in something that's mutually beneficial for all parties involved. This may have been the term Dragons of the East was trying to go for, but there's no way to know. <br /> I feel I should point out that what Dragons of the East did in having the Japanese originating Saensaeng move to Korea and take after WW2 and be largely made up of militaristic generals believing in supremacy of Japanese culture (and possibly race) is the sort of thing that is likely to be extremely offensive to most Koreans. The Japanese treatment of Korea when it was their colonial property, especially during WW2, is still a major issue in their relations. While not quite as bad as having Israel's branch of the Technocracy be run by a conspiracy of German supremacists who happened to show up in 1945, it's pretty close. <br /> <br /> With the Miao Guan, there's a GuanMiao district in southern Taiwan. I think - but am honestly not sure - that it's somehow supposed to mean Temple Barrier or something along those lines.<br /> For Taiping Tianguo, Taiping apparently translates as &quot;great peace&quot; or something to that effect. Tianguo apparently means Heaven. <br /> For Zi Guang, apparently guang means light. I think Zi may mean &quot;from&quot;, but I'm not certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:25:51-07:00","id":1388813,"title":"","content":"My theory is that while the Union as a whole is globalist, the Elemental Dragons are closet nationalists. They're not hiding their <i>existence</i> from the rest of the Union (that notion, as pointed out in TR, is stupid); but they <i>are</i> hiding their <i>agenda</i>, which is to establish China as <i>the</i> dominant world power. <br /> <br /> To that end, the Yellow/Earth Dragons are fine with the rest of the Union seeking a globalist agenda, as it's much easier to subvert a single governing structure to serve one country's interests than it is to have to dominate countries one by one. They're also very big on developing and deploying the Social Credit system by which they seek to control the Chinese population, and eventually the world population. <br /> <br /> The White/Metal Dragons are behind China's efforts to become the leaders in 5G and AI technologies, with the idea being that if China is manufacturing all of the hardware for the next-generation Internet, the Dragons will be able to insert backdoors at the hardware level greatly enhancing their ability to monitor and manipulate everything in the upcoming Internet of Things. In short, they seek to dominate the Digital Web. <br /> <br /> The Black/Water Dragons aren't just involved in organized crime; they're also the driving force behind China's One Belt/One Road policy, where China has been making lavish loans to impoverished countries, bankrolling massive infrastructure programs; and when the countries in question are unable to pay back the loans, China seizes the assets. In this way, the Black/Water Dragons are helping plant Chinese bases around the globe. They've also been instrumental, in cooperation with the Yellow/Earth Dragons, in building up China's technology through state policies that steal copyrights out from under businesses that seek to do business in China \u2014 essentially state-sanctioned corporate espionage. <br /> <br /> The Red/Fire Dragons are doing what they can to arm and staff those bases with the most advanced technology possible. They've also been involved in geo-engineering projects like the creation of artificial islands in the South China Sea in a land-grab (well, sea-grab) effort. They're also seeking to develop China's space program with the goal of being able to eliminate rival nations' satellite networks and achieve Space Superiority when the time comes. <br /> <br /> The Green/Wood Dragons have been developing China's bio-warfare capabilities. It's not known whether they're behind the current global pandemic (deliberately or not); but it's possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-15-2020, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T03:42:37-07:00","id":1388875,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I disagree with your theory, but it\u2019s both valid and interesting<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> I REALLY don\u2019t like that part in Dragons of the East about the Saensaeng in Korea. I had totally forgotten about that. Thanks.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that the Saensaeng began in Heian Japan (where they were known as the Court of Chrysanthemums, which actually is Japan\u2019s imperial flower), then they spread into Korea in the 13th century (where they became known as the Saensaeng).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T04:52:33-07:00","id":1388880,"title":"","content":"If someone wants to translate or question about Chinese, call me, as a Chinese l understand our language better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-16-2020, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T05:04:58-07:00","id":1388882,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a> thanks. Can you explain what \u201cTaiping Tianguo\u201d means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:10:31-07:00","id":1388905,"title":"","content":"Thanks all of you for your comments in this thread. Quite enlightening and interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:21:41-07:00","id":1388907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388882#post1388882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a> thanks. Can you explain what \u201cTaiping Tianguo\u201d means?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Taiping Tianguo(\u592a\u5e73\u5929\u56fd), Taiping Kingdom of Heaven, or Taiping Heavenly Kingdom in English, is originally a Chinese unrecognized oppositional state which was led by Hong Xiuquan from 1851 to1864 and dedicated </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">to overthrow the Qing Dynasty</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, but it failed at last</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-16-2020, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:37:34-07:00","id":1388913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused#post1386870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read Technocracy Reloaded and I\u2019m really confused. Are the Five Elemental Dragons a good thing (because they show how different the Asian Technocracy is from its Western counterpart) or a bad thing (because they\u2019re stereotypes of Asians)?<br /> <br /> I might use them in a Mage game someday and the only East Asian guy in our group is Filipino and he was born in the US and doesn\u2019t really know or care either way and I just want it to be authentic. Please help if you have any advice. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Filipino and I liked the Dragons of the East book. The initial appearance of the Five Elemental Dragons and the defining of the rest of the Technocracy as the Five Metal Dragons was interesting but the other books after seemed to ignore it which missed the whole point of fleshing them out in the Dragons of the East book. It was a cool idea and I'm glad they are finally fleshing things out with the other Organizations around the world that joined the Technocracy, I always wanted more of that. I think back to the Jonathan Hickman Shield Miniseries and it is great inspiration for how a Global Order of Reason style conspiracy would form around the globe, and be divided into roughly two halves, and eastern and western half.<br /> <br /> And I remember learning about Zaibatsu's in Japanese History class in Uni, they used the term because it is very iconic, you will notice in things like Anime and Manga they treat Zaibatsu's as like Mega Corporations like how you would define Pentex if it was in a comic. Like if you play Tekken they have the Mishima Zaibatsu and its treated like a Global Megacorp centered around the direct line of the Mishima family, fully under the control of Heihachi Mishima, and then his son Kazuma. The authors were definitely drawing upon the iconic usage of the term, its much like how the term Syndicate is also used in Comics and Manga for Criminal Enterprises with a seemingly legitimate face.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:44:38-07:00","id":1388914,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:50:44-07:00","id":1388918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388882#post1388882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24560_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24560\" data-vbnamecard=\"24560\">Rock113</a> thanks. Can you explain what \u201cTaiping Tianguo\u201d means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm assuming Tianguo would be Heaven country, if they had the characters I would be more certain. And the Taiping were one of the many rebellions, they were in the 1800's and had some religious/mystic doings, so I can see that if some of the Western Technocracy were religious factions that transitioned more into science, maybe the Taiping are something similar, how are they described, I forgot its been a while since I read Dragons of the East. But I think the characters for Taiping were great peace. So maybe they societal themed group, maybe a mix between NWO and cultish motifs?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oooph I got ninjaed by Rock!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  Opp Got Ninjaed 05-16-2020, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:56:02-07:00","id":1388922,"title":"","content":"Interesting. You think the Taiping Tianguo and the Taiping Rebellion are connected? I hadn\u2019t thought of that, but it does fit with my version of the Five Elemental Dragons. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:07:06-07:00","id":1388926,"title":"","content":"Oh its one group/Phrase the Taiping Tianguo, so yeah I guess that would be the Great Peace of the Heavenly Kingdom. I'm guessing if not directly connected the same title of Taiping would at least be meant so you drew parallels to the group if you knew about them. I'll be more informed when I read it. :P<br /> <br /> Do any of the Five Elemental Dragons use the Term Taipan? That feels like it would be in their lexicon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:09:22-07:00","id":1388927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388875#post1388875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I disagree with your theory, but it\u2019s both valid and interesting</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, everything I attribute to the Elemental Dragons is rooted in fact: China is in fact doing these things. Granted, that may be reason <i>not</i> to attribute them to the Elemental Dragons, especially since they <i>are</i> described as being broader-based than any one nation. But that raises its own concerns, such as what if anything they're doing with or about China's activities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388875#post1388875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I REALLY don\u2019t like that part in Dragons of the East about the Saensaeng in Korea. I had totally forgotten about that. Thanks.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that the Saensaeng began in Heian Japan (where they were known as the Court of Chrysanthemums, which actually is Japan\u2019s imperial flower), then they spread into Korea in the 13th century (where they became known as the Saensaeng).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main lesson to be taken away from No One of Consequence's post is that the names given in Dragons of the East are essentially made up, and are probably not worth keeping. I think that's what TR was getting at when it ridiculed the \u201cTaiping Tianguo\u201d name as something a Convention would adopt. <br /> <br /> Note that TR has also reshuffled some of the designations and retconned a lot of material: while you can probably keep much of the stuff about the Wood Dragons and Water Dragons (and even with the latter, I have some concerns), the other three are significantly revised. As near as I can tell, the group that was previously referred to as the Miao Guan is now the Yellow/Earth Dragons; what was originally the Earth Dragons (formerly the Saensaeng) are now the Red/Fire Dragons; and what was originally the Fire Dragons (a.k.a. the Zaibatsu) are now the White/Metal Dragons. Given that the Zaibatsu were associated with Matter and the Saensaeng were associated with Forces, I tend to prefer these revised associations. It also scraps the original notion that \u201cMetal Dragons\u201d is the Elemental Dragons' name for the Western Technocracy, and opens up the possibility of using \u201cSpirit Dragons\u201d as a designation for the Wu Lung. <br /> <br /> That said, a case could be made that most or all of the Elemental Dragons should also have Prime as an associated Sphere, given their shared interest in Chi. Metaphysically, that more than anything else distinguishes them from their Western counterparts. On the other hand, it may also be the aspect from Dragons of the East that most needs to be toned down: the whole Year of the Lotus seemed to be obsessed with Chi. And while the Dragons of the East aren't technically part of the Year of the Lotus, it's pretty much the same mindset. I also think the Technocratic Sphere variants should feature among the Dragons of the East, with the Yellow/Earth Dragons and White/Metal Dragons getting Data, the Red/Fire Dragons getting Dimensional Science, and the Black/Water Dragons getting Primal Utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:14:58-07:00","id":1388929,"title":"","content":"Good point. Like I said, I can\u2019t speak a word of Chinese, so I assumed the similar names were just a coincidence.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Dragons of the East uses the world Taipan, but I DO know what it means. It\u2019s like a tycoon, a powerful businessperson. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:23:29-07:00","id":1388932,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I agree. You\u2019ve got a point. I\u2019m gonna use the Dragon names from TR (apparently the old Asian-sounding names don\u2019t really mean anything, plus Zaibatsu is anachronistic). I also like the revised Sphere associations in TR. I am gonna keep the origin story though. I like the idea of the Dragons having a rich history that dates back long before the arrival of the European Order of Reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:28:27-07:00","id":1388934,"title":"","content":"Oh, absolutely. I like the notion that the modern Technocracy can actually trace its history back to <i>several</i> origins, with the Order of Reason and the Elemental Dragons being two of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:30:27-07:00","id":1388936,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> perfect \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> I usually prefer the Traditions, but TR is really helping me get a feel for the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:36:20-07:00","id":1388939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388929#post1388929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. Like I said, I can\u2019t speak a word of Chinese, so I assumed the similar names were just a coincidence.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Dragons of the East uses the world Taipan, but I DO know what it means. It\u2019s like a tycoon, a powerful businessperson. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and the Novel Taipan made the word more common kinda everywhere. I could see them referring to foreign high ranking technocrats as Taipans, or Syndicate Mob Bosses.<br /> <br /> I'm texting my old roommate some questions about connotations, we always helped each other edit things between our languages even after we moved to different cities. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:40:23-07:00","id":1388941,"title":"","content":"Oh interesting Dataweaver, so if the Wu Lung are the Spirit Dragons that gives the impression of a connected willworker society in ancient China/Asia, and the rise of Science had their more esoteric group split off.<br /> <br /> Okay it clears up so much confusion by getting rid of the five metal dragons and making just one group the metal dragons. I always confused the term Metal Dragons and Elemental Dragons. :P<br /> <br /> I agree they should used the Techi Spheres like Data.<br /> <br /> Its interesting that they kept the chi focus, that makes me think the other technocratic groups outside of Europe may have odd philosophical/paradigm quirks.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I finally backed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:35:00-07:00","id":1388969,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> awesome! \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> good point. Better to get rid of the term \u201cFive Metal Dragons\u201d altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T10:03:12-07:00","id":1388978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388934#post1388934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, absolutely. I like the notion that the modern Technocracy can actually trace its history back to <i>several</i> origins, with the Order of Reason and the Elemental Dragons being two of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own head canon has what grew out of the late Medieval Order of Reason and the ancient Chinese Ministry of Works (as well as Japan's Court of the Chrysanthemum and Court of the Plum Blossom mentioned in Guide to the Traditions) eventually melding - at least in the sense of the Ministry and Courts adapting Western technology and other trappings while still pursing their own ends that just happen to be really similar to that of the Union - in the 19th and early 20th century. Meanwhile, in the Middle East, you have elements of the Collectors of Light and even parts of the Ahl I Batin who have adapted the Union's tools and methods and are Technocrats, but they've been heavily hampered by the Righteous Brethren of Purity and Submission (an offshoot of the Cabal of Pure Thought), who hate Western modernity as much as they hate the heretical Traditions and Crafts of the Web of Faith. I suspect if I did enough research, I could build a case for India having its own counterpart of the Elemental/Metal Dragons.<br /> <br /> As for the term Five Metal Dragons, I think it actually works fairly well as a name that other Chinese supernaturals - mages, the Beast Courts, the Yellow Springs, the Hsien, etc. - refer to them as, probably in a slightly disparaging tone. The group itself likely still thinks of itself as the true Ministry of Works just updated to the modern age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-16-2020, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T10:54:04-07:00","id":1388989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388922#post1388922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. You think the Taiping Tianguo and the Taiping Rebellion are connected? I hadn\u2019t thought of that, but it does fit with my version of the Five Elemental Dragons. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is: Yes. They do have a great connection, Taiping Tianguo started, led and dominated the whole Taiping Rebellion. It is not a coincidence. Although this Rebellion failed and Tianguo collapsed, it hit Qing Dynasty so heavily that sentenced it to death indirectly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-16-2020, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T13:52:44-07:00","id":1389061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388978#post1388978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own head canon has what grew out of the late Medieval Order of Reason and the ancient Chinese Ministry of Works (as well as Japan's Court of the Chrysanthemum and Court of the Plum Blossom mentioned in Guide to the Traditions) eventually melding - at least in the sense of the Ministry and Courts adapting Western technology and other trappings while still pursing their own ends that just happen to be really similar to that of the Union - in the 19th and early 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go a step further and say that sometime in the 20th century, probably in the aftermath of World War II, the Elemental Dragons formally join with the Technocratic Union. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388978#post1388978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, in the Middle East, you have elements of the Collectors of Light and even parts of the Ahl I Batin who have adapted the Union's tools and methods and are Technocrats, but they've been heavily hampered by the Righteous Brethren of Purity and Submission (an offshoot of the Cabal of Pure Thought), who hate Western modernity as much as they hate the heretical Traditions and Crafts of the Web of Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div> To me, Technocrats has a much more focused meaning. Is be willing to call the Collectors of Light \u201cScientists\u201d; but to be a Technocrat, you need to couple this with the belief that they, as technical experts, can and should run society. The Ministry of Works certainly held such beliefs; I'm not so sure the Collectors of Light did. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388978#post1388978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect if I did enough research, I could build a case for India having its own counterpart of the Elemental/Metal Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But when TR was announced back near the end of the M20 KS, there was mention that it would include an African Technocracy. As with what we're discussing about the Elemental Dragons, I'd love to see what the native origins of the Technocracy in Africa would have been like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388978#post1388978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the term Five Metal Dragons, I think it actually works fairly well as a name that other Chinese supernaturals - mages, the Beast Courts, the Yellow Springs, the Hsien, etc. - refer to them as, probably in a slightly disparaging tone. The group itself likely still thinks of itself as the true Ministry of Works just updated to the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That said, TR makes a point that another reason to reject the canned names from DotE is that the Far East is a very diverse region with multiple cultures and multiple languages, and naming schemes vary from place to place. If there's a region in the East where they have something like the Western alchemical notion of significant metals, you could end up with something like the Golden Dragons, the Silver Dragons, the Iron Dragons, and so on, as one of the naming schemes. Mind you, that's a big if.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:29:39-07:00","id":1389107,"title":"","content":"Technocracy in Africa could run through many threads, because vast civilizations require a lot of organization and technology. There's probably a claim to Technocrats all the way back in Egypt for the historical period, and some Void Engineer-influenced member of the Collegium of History might say the first Technocrats were the hominids who made tools and invented language.<br /> <br /> Basically, with a little research and some sensitivity, many studies in African civilization could be done for Technocracy Reloaded. If the authors lack the expertise, a supplement on the native roots of the African Technocracy in more detail would be a great Storyteller's Vault item.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T17:55:12-07:00","id":1389129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1389061#post1389061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go a step further and say that sometime in the 20th century, probably in the aftermath of World War II, the Elemental Dragons formally join with the Technocratic Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably place it a little earlier, between the Xinhai Revolution in 1911 and Japanese invasion of Manchuria in 1931, with the establishment of the Republic of China and its efforts on modernization. Of course, there's probably a disagreement of opinion between those favoring Mao's version of Marxism and those favoring Sun Yat-sen's Three Principles of the People, with the former winning out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, Technocrats has a much more focused meaning. Is be willing to call the Collectors of Light \u201cScientists\u201d; but to be a Technocrat, you need to couple this with the belief that they, as technical experts, can and should run society. The Ministry of Works certainly held such beliefs; I'm not so sure the Collectors of Light did. </div> </div> </div>I should probably clarify that, at least in my own head canon, a number of the groups in the Web of Faith tend to cross the lines between Traditions as usually classified, probably owing to the influence of the Batini's Doctrine of Unity and continuous subtle efforts to bring everyone together. So much in the same way as I have the Darwushim as a group effectively being part of the Batini, the Ecstatics and the Akashic Brotherhood all at the same time, I tend to view the Collectors of Light being this group that is - or was - effectively part of the Batini University of Light, part of the Celestial Chorus's Alexandrian Society, early Artificers/Order of Reason members, and perhaps even on the fringes of the Solificati and later part of the Sons of Ether, with various members breaking different ways after the collapse of the Ottoman Empire and the Batini leaving the Traditions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps. But when TR was announced back near the end of the M20 KS, there was mention that it would include an African Technocracy. As with what we're discussing about the Elemental Dragons, I'd love to see what the native origins of the Technocracy in Africa would have been like. </div> </div> </div>I know Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade has some discussion about Mali and it's association with the Order of Reason. <br /> With Africa, you are sort of talking about four or five different regions. North Africa/Egypt, which is part of the Mediterranean and Muslim worlds; West Africa, with things like the Mali, Songhay, Great Fulo and other Empires, many of which were either connected to the Islamic world or later Portuguese traders; East Africa, which includes the ancient Aksum/modern Ethiopia and the various Swahili city states along the coast, again part of the edges of the Islamic world; and Southern Africa, with the Kingdoms of Zimbabwe, Kongo, Matamba, and Maravi, among others. I can't really guess which ones would be most likely to have surviving secret societies as part of the modern Union. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agreed. That said, TR makes a point that another reason to reject the canned names from DotE is that the Far East is a very diverse region with multiple cultures and multiple languages, and naming schemes vary from place to place. </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I like to present the Chinese and Japanese parts of the Technocracy as being two different things, each with their own unique history prior to joining the Union and their own internal cultures, outlooks and goals. Likewise the ones in the Koreas, Thailand, Vietnam and so on. By the same token, I like to insert little bits about the same sometimes happening in places like Britain (with the Harbingers of Avalon), France, Germany, Scandinavia, and Russia, as well as parts of Latin America and even sometimes regions of North America, sometimes with holdovers from the old Order of Reason days or sooner, or just reflecting certain strongly ingrained cultural aspects. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:03:28-07:00","id":1389131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386870-five-elemental-dragons-really-frustrated-and-confused?p=1388989#post1388989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is: Yes. They do have a great connection, Taiping Tianguo started, led and dominated the whole Taiping Rebellion. It is not a coincidence. Although this Rebellion failed and Tianguo collapsed, it hit Qing Dynasty so heavily that sentenced it to death indirectly</div> </div> </div> </div>Some nations have a bad year or even a bad decade. China, between about 1840 and 1945, had a very bad century. (And following that up with Mao's famines and the Cultural Revolution didn't exactly make things better.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T15:37:07-07:00","id":1389478,"title":"","content":"I like the statement of the book that the Technocracy is probably 3-1 Asian, it's just that the Americans tend to assume they're the majority because they're Americans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a>